Comment (internal/service/llm/anthropic_test.go:156):
**[Medium] This passthrough test gives false confidence about unsupported schema keywords.**

The schema under test deliberately includes `minLength` (line 125) and `minimum` (line 128) — keywords Anthropic structured outputs do not support. But the test asserts the schema round-trips byte-for-byte against an `httptest` fake that echoes success regardless of payload, so it proves the wire shape, not that the **real** API accepts such a schema. As written, it reads as "schemas with min/max constraints work," which is the opposite of the likely live behavior (400).

Pair this with the schema-stripping fix on `anthropic.go`: once the client sanitizes the schema, assert here that the unsupported keywords were *removed* from the outgoing `format.schema`.
