Comment (internal/config/config.go:216):
**[Low] AI config validation fatals at startup even when AI is disabled.**

`LoadAIConfig()` → `Validate()` rejects any provider other than `anthropic`, and a failure here calls `logger.Fatalw`, aborting boot. That means a typo or leftover `CCF_AI_PROVIDER` takes down the **entire app** even with `CCF_AI_ENABLED=false` and no intent to use AI at all.

Suggestion: skip provider validation when `!cfg.Enabled` (validate only the enabled path), so a misconfigured-but-disabled AI block does not block unrelated startup.
