Comment (internal/service/llm/anthropic.go:80):
**[Low] `MaxTokens` is not defaulted.**

If a caller leaves `StructuredRequest.MaxTokens` at its zero value, this sends `max_tokens: 0`, which the API rejects with a 400 → mapped to `ErrInvalidOutput` (non-retryable). For a shared client this is an easy footgun. Consider defaulting to a sane value (mirroring the model/timeout defaulting already done in `NewAnthropicClient`) when `req.MaxTokens <= 0`, or validating it up front with a clearer error.
